  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Life-Saving Humanitarian Assistance to Vulnerable Migrants who Crossed the Darien</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">During this twelfth-month project, International Organization for Migration (IOM) aims to respond to the humanitarian needs of migrants, particularly those who have crossed the Darien jungle, are in transit or stranded in government-managed migrant reception centers and to contribute to improving institutional capacities and conditions of the migrant reception centers. As well as in remote reception communities in the indigenous Comarca Embera Wounaan that are the main transit points. IOM is providing essential services and assistance to improve their living conditions and dignity, reduce migrants suffering and avoid loss of life. This multi-sectoral action includes providing access to food, health, essential non-food items, and protection assistance; and improving reception and temporally collective centers conditions. Camp Coordination and Camp management (CCCM) will be part of the activities such as regular visits and facilitate CCCM refresher trainings for humanitariann staff and government partners.</narrative>
  </description>
